108-## Theorem and local-proof obligations
109-
110-Each item below needs its own complete argument or a named physical postulate/source-backed experiment with no fictitious proof. The table states proof obligations, not established category results.
111-
112-| Proposed result | Required inputs and proof work | Failure if omitted |
113-|---|---|---|
114:| Defect charge/deformation theorem | A precise current equation or an axiomatically supplied topological defect; Stokes’ theorem on an interpolating chain disjoint from charged insertions; contact terms at operator insertions; boundary terms and current improvements; specified support regularity. | A slogan that “conserved current means symmetry” does not prove a topological defect in the quantum model. |
115-| Finite 2-group background consistency | \(G,A,\rho,\beta\), normalized cocycle, twisted cochains and cup products, explicit degree conventions, and gauge transformations. Verify the cocycle condition, closure, composition, and invariance of \(\delta_a B=a^*\beta\). | Confusing the Postnikov coupling with an anomaly, omitting local coefficients, or using an untwisted \(\delta\) invalidates the background. |
116:| Categorical fusion/defect realization | The actual QFT or finite lattice Hamiltonian; construction of every defect operator; junction vector spaces; associator maps and pentagon; orientation reversal/adjoints; proof of isotopy invariance and of the claimed fusion coefficients. | Abstract fusion-category axioms or a transfer matrix do not show that any given QFT has those defects. |
117-| Finite gauging/gluing | The exact finite field groupoid and automorphism weights; cocycle action and triangulation convention; gauge invariance; gluing/sewing; boundary data and orientation signs. | A raw sum over field representatives can overcount gauge-equivalent data or fail to be local under gluing. |
118-| Perturbative anomaly/counterterm theorem | The selected non-Abelian action, fermion representations, local BRST differential, scheme/regulator and quantum Ward identity; prove the anomaly is a local cocycle and identify allowed counterterms; fix the invariant polynomial and descent normalization. | The current Abelian scalar proposition assumes locality/nilpotence/allowed counterterms and proves only an abstract obstruction equivalence. It does not prove a quantum action principle or identify the physical coefficient. |
119-| Global anomaly test | A specified gauge group/global form, bundle topology, spin structure, gauge transformation loop/component, fermion determinant/Pfaffian and its regularization; evaluate the resulting phase (eta invariant, index-flow, or explicit determinant line). | Vanishing local \(I_{d+2}\) does not imply absence of a global anomaly; ordinary real Chern–Weil forms miss integral torsion. |
120:| Bulk inflow cancellation | Same backgrounds and cochain/differential conventions on the boundary and bulk; exact variation under all allowed small and large transformations; show bulk-boundary phase cancellation and compatibility with gluing. | A formal local descent cancellation cannot by itself cancel a torsion phase or a defect-junction anomaly. |
121-| Anomaly matching / IR constraint | Prove anomaly-class invariance under the stated RG map; state whether the symmetry is unbroken; specify whether a topological sector or relative boundary theory is admitted. Then rule out only the particular proposed IR realization. | “Anomaly matching forbids a trivial gap” is false without the unbroken-symmetry, locality, gap, degeneracy, and topological-order qualifications. |
122:| Supersymmetric defect anomaly | A physical real superalgebra and preserved subalgebra; exact defect coupling and background supergravity/R fields; a supersymmetric regulator/current multiplet; complete anomaly/inflow computation. | A bare complex superalgebra or non-supersymmetric anomaly polynomial does not furnish a supersymmetric defect theorem. |
