124:For finite bosonic ordinary group-like symmetries, a \(U(1)\)-valued \((d+1)\)-cocycle can define a Dijkgraaf–Witten-type invertible action. That is a clean intermediate result if its triangulated model is fixed. It is not the full anomaly classification for spin theories, continuous groups, higher-form symmetries, nontrivial spacetime structures, or noninvertible defects. For general invertible anomaly theories, use a specified bordism-spectrum/Anderson-dual or differential-cohomology formulation; do not assert that all anomalies are characters of one ordinary bordism group without stating the exact theory category and target.
