156-## Research questions to preserve as open frontier, not suppliers
157-
158:1. **Higher-dimensional categorical anomaly classification.** For a fixed unitary fusion 2-category of codimension-one defects in a 3+1D theory, specify which background/junction data are gaugeable modulo local 4D counterterms and whether the complete obstruction is represented by a 4+1D invertible theory for the fixed tangential structure. The finite \(\mathrm{Vec}_G^\omega\) and \(2\mathrm{Vect}_G^\omega\) algebraic models are examples, not a universal answer.
159:2. **Continuous noninvertible symmetries outside 1+1D CFT.** Extend a precise current/defect construction and prove topologicality, fusion, RG behavior, anomaly/background coupling, and the distinction between intrinsic and “invertible up to gauging” cases. The 2025 article’s conclusion directly identifies higher-dimensional generalization and background coupling as open directions.
160-3. **Lattice-to-continuum gauging interfaces.** Reconcile movement of finite-regulator constraints/interfaces with continuum background gauge transformations, higher-form symmetry and boundary anomaly inflow. The 2026 lattice interface preprint supplies finite examples, not a universal continuum theorem.
161-4. **Generalized family anomalies.** Determine when a parameter-space family with explicit symmetry breaking can be treated as a higher/categorical family, and which anomaly data constrain every point of an RG flow or only the family as a whole. The 2026 JHEP paper studies selected models; do not extrapolate its examples without their assumptions.
162:5. **Supersymmetric defect anomalies.** For a named 4D \(\mathcal N=2\) or 6D \(\mathcal N=(1,0)\) SCFT and a selected half-BPS surface defect, derive the defect anomaly polynomial, supersymmetric background completion, and relation to a Casimir-energy or Rényi observable. The October 2026 arXiv lead’s abstract makes this a timely interface; the full paper and its status must be read before using any formula.
163-6. **Spin/global anomaly computation.** Build the explicit bridge from a selected chiral QFT determinant line/eta phase to an exact spin-\(G\) bordism-spectrum invariant, including torsion and mixed higher-form backgrounds. The current root spin/Dirac page supplies geometric spin and index prerequisites but not this anomaly map.
164:7. **3+1D and mixed-state categories.** Separate pure-state QFT anomalies from mixed-state topological orders. The 2026 braided-fusion-2-category realization preprint is a current lead whose body/proofs are not covered here; do not import its abstract as a theorem.
