items/ex-qsmx-double-z2.md:49:Assume the Axiom of Choice for the stated lattice prerequisite. Let $\mathbb Z_2=\{e,s\}$ with $s^2=e$. Its finite-group double has exactly four irreducible complex sectors, each one-dimensional: the two conjugacy-class labels (flux labels) $e,s$ paired with the two group characters $\chi_\pm:\mathbb Z_2\to\mathbb C^\times$ with $\chi_\pm(e)=1$ and $\chi_\pm(s)=\pm1$. Here the conjugacy-class label $C$ is the magnetic-flux label and the centralizer-representation class $[\pi]$ is the electric-charge label; these are names for the algebraic labels. In particular, the nontrivial charge character evaluated on the nontrivial flux is $-1$, equal to the commutation sign for one crossing of a closed primal $Z$ string with a closed dual $X$ string on the square $L\times L$ torus for $L\ge3$.
