3. **Lattice-to-continuum gauging interfaces.** Reconcile movement of finite-regulator constraints/interfaces with continuum background gauge transformations, higher-form symmetry and boundary anomaly inflow. The 2026 lattice interface preprint supplies finite examples, not a universal continuum theorem.
4. **Generalized family anomalies.** Determine when a parameter-space family with explicit symmetry breaking can be treated as a higher/categorical family, and which anomaly data constrain every point of an RG flow or only the family as a whole. The 2026 JHEP paper studies selected models; do not extrapolate its examples without their assumptions.
