Next action: author the normalized $\mathbb Z_2$ 3-cocycle associator example, then reconcile the complete B inventory and proof contracts.

## Completed item: `ex-aqft-fusion-z2-twisted-associator`

Claim and conventions: for $G=\mathbb Z_2$, $\omega(a,b,c)=(-1)^{abc}$ is normalized and satisfies the multiplicative 3-cocycle identity. The associated graded-vector-space category has two simple objects, fusion $\delta_a\otimes\delta_b\cong\delta_{a+b}$, and an associator scalar $-1$ on $(\delta_1,\delta_1,\delta_1)$; the untwisted package has the same multiplicities and scalar $+1$. The item explicitly does not claim that the two categories are inequivalent. Dependencies: `def-aqft-noninvertible-defect-fusion` and `def-monoidal-category`; `dependency_level: 1`.

Source context: Etingof et al., *Tensor Categories*, Example 2.3.8 and §4.1, full author-hosted PDF <https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/egnobookfinal.pdf>. The source gives the cocycle-twisted associator construction; the $\mathbb Z_2$ exponent identity, normalization, duality, and comparison of associator components are checked locally. No continuum or physical interpretation is claimed. Scoped checks and source-fetch stamping remain pending.

Next action: finish the manifest, A/B frontmatter, proof contracts, source coverage, and batch dependency record; then run the required scoped validators and readiness recording.

## Completed item: `ex-aqft-fusion-z2-twisted-associator`

Claim and conventions: the normalized function $\omega(a,b,c)=(-1)^{abc}$ on additive $\mathbb Z_2$ satisfies the 3-cocycle equation. Its graded-vector-space category has fusion rule $\delta_a\otimes\delta_b\cong\delta_{a+b}$ and associator $-1$ on $(\delta_1,\delta_1,\delta_1)$; the untwisted data have identical multiplicities but associator $+1$. No monoidal inequivalence claim is made. Dependencies are `def-aqft-noninvertible-defect-fusion` and `def-monoidal-category`; `dependency_level: 1`.

Source context: Etingof et al., *Tensor Categories*, Example 2.3.8, printed pp. 27–28, and §4.1, printed pp. 65–66, full author-hosted PDF <https://math.mit.edu/~etingof/egnobookfinal.pdf>. The cocycle identity, normalization, pentagon, unit triangle, duality and comparison of fusion coefficients versus associator values are checked locally. The finite $\mathbb Z_2$ cocycle equation is an exact algebraic check on all four variables. Source-fetch stamping and final formatting checks remain pending.

